---
/**
 * ZineSurface - the QUIET plate grammar: a card lifted off the page with a 1px
 * zinc edge, carrying the grunge ink at its edge.
 *
 * THE SECOND PLATE GRAMMAR. `ZineBox` is the LOUD one - a 4px crimson module
 * boundary and a hard offset shadow. This is the quiet one: the ground a module
 * sits on rather than the frame around it. They are not variants of each other,
 * and neither is a substitute for the other.
 *
 * Why the idiom is a component and not a class pair: `.shell-card` (the surface)
 * and `.grunge` (the texture) are two published atoms, but the SHAPE is three
 * facts that must agree - the surface, the texture, and the painter hook
 * (`data-grunge` + `data-grunge-mode`) the grunge script reads. A page that
 * writes the two classes and forgets the hook gets an empty plate with no ink
 * and no error anywhere, which is why the combination is stated once, here.
 *
 * WHAT IT REPLACED. Fifty-four sites across ten pages hand-wrote
 * `<div class="grunge shell-card ..." data-grunge data-grunge-mode="edge">` before
 * this file existed, and forty-seven of them now render through it. Each one
 * renders identically: the class list is `grunge shell-card` plus whatever
 * `Class` carries, in that order, and the two data attributes are the ones the
 * pages already wrote.
 *
 * NOT FOR AN `<article>`. The element this renders is a `<div>`, because Astro
 * cannot render a dynamic tag name (`<Tag>` compiles to a component lookup, not
 * an element). A surface that is a self-contained composition - a card whose
 * semantics matter to a reader or an outline - keeps its own `<article>` and
 * composes `.grunge .shell-card` itself. The seven sites still literal are
 * exactly those; see `Documentation/DesignSystem.md` for the register.
 */
interface Props {
	/** Extra classes for the surface itself: spacing, width, flex, a shadow. */
	Class?: string;

	/** The grunge painter's mode. `edge` rings the plate's border (the default
	 *  the pages wrote); `scatter` sprinkles the ink across it. Omitted leaves
	 *  the painter on its own default. */
	Mode?: "edge" | "scatter";

	/** An anchor id, for a surface the section index links to. */
	Id?: string;

	/** A one-off inline style. RESERVED for a data-driven value (a custom
	 *  property the page computes); a fixed value belongs in the sheet. */
	Style?: string;
}

const { Class = "", Mode, Id, Style } = Astro.props;
---

<div
	class:list={["grunge", "shell-card", Class]}
	id={Id}
	style={Style}
	data-grunge
	data-grunge-mode={Mode}
>
	<slot />
</div>
